{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1527479-true-faith-and-changeling","id":1527479,"title":"True Faith and Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-26T20:03:06-08:00","id":1527479,"title":"True Faith and Changeling","content":"I looked everywhere(Almost) and i still can't find anything about what true faith does on changeling. I am making a chronicle and one of my characters has true faith and one of them is a changeling and the question came to me : What does it do on a changeling? Anyone knows? (Using 20th anniversary rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight","name":"CastleNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T22:00:27-08:00","id":1527481,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's much written about it. Even the 1995 sourcebook The Inquisition lacks a section on True Faith versus Changelings despite addressing the other four splats (I assume Changeling hadn't been published yet). So you'll need to decide yourself.<br /> <br /> Folklore does offer some suggestions. Many fairies don't like church bells and will flee from them. Baptism of newborns will prevent changelings. Pages from the Bible, making the sign of the cross, and invoking the saints are often just as effective as iron. Some fairies express an interest in becoming Christian, or worry that they cannot have eternal life like Christian humans because they are fairy. But how do you want to translate that into the game? Just substitute fairy for vampire in the True Faith rules? Make it an intrinsic flaw like iron that requires a Merit to negate? Make it available as a Flaw? Treat is as some kind of Banality? Something else? Different STs will take different tacks depending on their own understanding and bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T00:19:41-08:00","id":1527483,"title":"","content":"I have (very) faint memories about reading <i>something</i> regarding faith/true faith and the Changelings in <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b><br /> Sadly at the moment it not possible to dig up my Dark Ages: Fae book to check it out - but if you have it, worth a shot<br /> Either that, or my mind played a trick on me<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T04:12:27-08:00","id":1527489,"title":"","content":"I think it should depend on the fae. House Liam for instance should be doing pretty well with regards to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T12:20:45-08:00","id":1527510,"title":"","content":"The Echoes flaw in the C20 book has some examples of what Black Fox describes being put into mechanical terms re: effects of interaction with church symbols and the like.<br /> <br /> I do think it would be worth further examination as a subject because it is an interesting field, interactions between Fey/changelings and True Faith type things. As noted there is plenty of European folklore that has to do with the fair folk being averse to the sign of the cross, Bible, church bells, etc. The stated reasons for this, either Watsonian or Doyalist, varies. There\u2019s an old idea that the fair folk are the angels who weren\u2019t bad enough to be condemned to Hell during Satan\u2019s Fall but weren\u2019t good enough to be allowed to stay in Heaven either, which might suggest why they react the way they do to symbols of the faith. Other researchers have likened it to something similar to how iron became associated with anti-Fey qualities; the hypothesis being that oral culture remembered the use of Roman/Christian iron to destroy old Druidic/pre-Christian religious and spiritual sites and that iron-as-modernization became anathema to the fair folk as they became associated with The Past\u2122\ufe0f. One could imagine then that Christianization could play a similar role; the force of the Present (Christianity in Medieval/Renaissance Europe) being used to overcome the (Pagan) Past. <br /> <br /> Other subjects of interest might also be the somewhat fluid boundaries between what is imagined as Fey or as Demonic. For instance, it wasn\u2019t unusual for saints in folklore to have power over demons (after all, King Solomon did it), yet sometimes these relationships would be recontextualized as saints with Fey type beings instead for any number of reasons (for example: St. Nicholas commanded demonic spirits, Santa Claus has elven helpers). Also to consider was the notion that Fey spirits could hypothetically become human through marriage/union with human beings (see certain genres of Animal Bride stories or Paracelsus\u2019 warning that many water-nymphs tempt Christian men into marriage in order to gain a soul before abandoning them). I\u2019m less familiar with Islamic or Buddhist folklore traditions but I believe they have similar phenomena of holy people commanding/exorcising nature spirits/tricksters/demons; so I\u2019d also be curious to see what role they could play into a larger discussion on this subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T16:38:47-08:00","id":1527523,"title":"","content":"I know it's not quite what you asked, but I think you can go the simpler way, a person who would have the state of true faith is so firmly a believer in their faith that they inevitably reject the existence of fairies and myths and therefore has a high banality or that as the mythology of each place affects changelings, any legend that they would have vulnerability to religious objects translates into weakness against true faith. In my opinion, I think the first one makes more sense when I stop to think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T04:25:01-08:00","id":1527544,"title":"","content":"Believing in the fae has nothing to do with Banality, at least not in C20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T15:42:50-08:00","id":1527641,"title":"","content":"You would have thought something like that would have been in Autumn People, but apparently not. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T16:14:05-08:00","id":1527642,"title":"","content":"It makes sense that it wasn't. True Faith and Banality don't mix. <br /> <br /> I <i>am</i> surprised that <b>The Inquisition</b> didn't address it; while <b>Changeling</b> was new at the time, it <i>was </i>out, as demonstrated by the fact that <b>Autumn People</b> was contemporaneous with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T07:38:35-08:00","id":1527655,"title":"","content":"Just thinking out loud here, but it feels like someone with True Faith might actually be prone to spawning their own guardian angel in stressful situations. Sure it's just a chimera, but it would be a nasty surprise for an unsuspecting changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T07:48:00-08:00","id":1527656,"title":"","content":"I really do think that True Faith would be orthogonal to questions of Banality and Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T19:35:46-08:00","id":1527732,"title":"","content":"In Dark Ages: Fae, the spread of the religion of the &quot;White Christ&quot;, and in particular, individuals with True Faith, are the major existential threat* that the Fae are suddenly waking up to after having been off doing their own thing for a few centuries. For example, Changeling babies who are baptized never grow up to be Fae.<br /> <br /> Faith can trigger Echoes (personal rather than kith-bases Frailties) which cause any number of unpleasant effects from mild inconvenience up through bodily immolation. Interestingly for this conversation, becoming Locked (we'd say Undone) is never one of them, but becoming immediately Lost (i.e. Bedlam) is one of the most severe. So in that sense, True Faith is more like a very powerful, alien Art than a force of Banality.<br /> <br /> In the Autumn World, Unleashing or otherwise Invoking the Wyrd causes a reflexive Banality backlash. So I think it would be generally sensible if &quot;attacking&quot; a Changeling with True Faith basically played out like forcing the fae to Unleash involuntarily, and suffer the consequences?<br /> <br /> *My (not-inconsistent-with-the-text) headcanon is that Christianity is different and scary because of the paradigm-for-Sleepers doctrine of &quot;salvation through faith alone&quot;, but I'm still a Mage guy at heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T19:35:46-08:00","id":1527733,"title":"","content":"In Dark Ages: Fae, the spread of the religion of the &quot;White Christ&quot;, and in particular, individuals with True Faith, are the major existential threat* that the Fae are suddenly waking up to after having been off doing their own thing for a few centuries. For example, Changeling babies who are baptized never grow up to be Fae.<br /> <br /> Faith can trigger Echoes (personal rather than kith-bases Frailties) which cause any number of unpleasant effects from mild inconvenience up through bodily immolation. Interestingly for this conversation, becoming Locked (we'd say Undone) is never one of them, but becoming immediately Lost (i.e. Bedlam) is one of the most severe. So in that sense, True Faith is more like a very powerful, alien Art than a force of Banality.<br /> <br /> In the Autumn World, Unleashing or otherwise Invoking the Wyrd causes a reflexive Banality backlash. So I think it would be generally sensible if &quot;attacking&quot; a Changeling with True Faith basically played out like forcing the fae to Unleash involuntarily, and suffer the consequences?<br /> <br /> *My (not-inconsistent-with-the-text) headcanon is that Christianity is different and scary because of the paradigm-for-Sleepers doctrine of &quot;salvation through faith alone&quot;, but I'm still a Mage guy at heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 01-02-2024, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T14:23:29-08:00","id":1527879,"title":"","content":"The mention of Mage gives me a notion of how one could potentially flesh out the use of Faith for their chronicles by pulling slightly from Mage and having either formal or informal \u2018resonance\u2019 tags associated with traits like Faith that would color how the trait interacts with Changelings.<br /> <br /> People have alluded to already how a 1-size-fits-all approach to Faith doesn\u2019t really suit incorporating the various ways that Faith (whether Christian, Muslim, Buddhist, etc.) effects Fey or Trickster I\u2019m in Trickster /Natural Spirits in folklore. One way of handling this could be to choose the elements that best suit the themes I of your chronicle and use those primarily for that chronicle. <br /> <br /> But on the other hand, going more off of a resonance like system, I would imagine something like:<br /> <br /> A Changeling encountering someone whose Faith is associated with their role as a Spiritual Warrior, whether the pagan-hunters of Antiquity or \u00e0 contemporary inquisitor, would be effected by their Faith in the typical fashion. That person\u2019s Faith attribute/True Faith could be used to represent their capacity for undoing chimerical effects, undoing enchantment, and even \u2018suppressing the Fey\u2019 (putting Changelings into a quasi-undone state; whether or not this is banality proper though is potentially up for debate.<br /> <br /> On the other extreme however, someone whose Faith is more akin to a Folk Mystic or Cunning Midwife, whether in their classical manifestations or as a contemporary reconstruction, might affect Changelings differently. They might be able to use their Faith to undo malignant chimerical effects but also empower benevolent chimerical effects. I can even imagine a category of Saint-figures whose Faith might be able to compel the Fey to a certain extent or even provide them a sort of \u2018Adoption\u2019 status. Perhaps those Fey spirits who, for example, consented to undergo a Christian baptism undertaken by a Saint-figure would be able to resist Faith-based banality/undoing but would receive a number of Oaths/Bans suited to the tenets of the Saint\u2019s Faith: for instance they might be forbidden from using their malignant powers against any Christian child or from tampering with a church\u2019s threshold or what have you. <br /> <br /> This could potentially be an interesting theme to add to the history of the Sundering/Shattering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T13:42:08-08:00","id":1528055,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all your answers! I will think about it. Because those changeling are tied to the dreaming, i am thinking that maybe the faith can block that dreaming in some way. I will make research about it and make a decision. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28291-castlenight","name":"CastleNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}